>  Hello,
        I am a student completing my bachelor degree.  I have a project
paper
        to be completed in my final semester.  

>  I am interested in using S-Plus to run my output (as we can get robust 
        estimates from the software, i.e., M-estimator and etc.  Therefore,
my 
        supervisor wants me to run the output using S-Plus).  Unfortunately,
I know
>  only the SAS commands.  Could some one out there help me?
>  
>  This is my program using SAS, could you please translate it to
> S-Language?
>  
>  Array S{10001} S1-S10001;
>  Array T{10001} T1-T10001;
>  C=0;
>  D=0;
>  S{1}=0.0;
>  T{1}=0.0;
>  Do I = 2 to 10001;
>  X1=RANNOR (316703);
>  X2=RANNOR (849081);
>  X3=RANNOR (551837);
>  X4=RANNOR (162309);
>  X5=RANNOR (795535);
>  Z= MEAN (X1-X5);
>  S{I} = MAX (0, S{I-1} + (Z-0.5/SQRT (5))*SQRT(5));
>  T{I} = MIN (0, T{I-1} + (Z+0.5/SQRT (5))*SQRT(5));
>  IF S{I} <3 THEN C=C+1;
>  ELSE S{I} =0;
>  IF T{I}>-3 THEN D=D+1;
>  ELSE T{I}=0;
>  END;
>  A=10000-C;
>  B=10000-D;
>  ARL=10000/(A+B);
>  OUTPUT;
>  PROC PRINT;
>  VAR ARL;
>  RUN;
>  
>  
>  Your help is much NEEDED and APPRECIATED.
>  Thank you.
>  
>  
>  
>  
>  Sincerely
>  Liow C.H.
>  
>  
>  
