hello all,
I'd like to read data from files that can contain both binary and ascii
data.
Binary data are stored after an header that describe their length and other
specificities. Those data can be coded on 1,3,4,or 8 octets.
I've wrote a C function to read data from the file using function "fread"
but after 1 day of various trys, I can't manage to get the data passed to
S-PLUS 2000 (MS-WIN98,PII-266,RAM64) without a crash.
Has anyone tried to do such things before? A piece of code or advices would
be very much appreciated.
I enclose the C code and the S-PLUS function below.
Thanks,

    Mathieu Ros

